          },
          "code": "PARSEDATA",
          "id": "1765585160622",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "errorNodeId": null,
            "name": "Create Actions"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "CREATE_ACTIONS",
          "id": "1765590580504",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765590580506_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are provided structured JSON user data containing:\n\n- Skill gaps: `{{$context.$nodes.PARSEDATA.$output.result.SkillGaps}}`\n- Recommended courses: `{{$context.$nodes.PARSEDATA.$output.result.RecommendedCourses}}`\n- Recommended gigs/opportunities: `{{$context.$nodes.PARSEDATA.$output.result.RecommendedGigs}}`\n\nAnalyze the recommendations and select up to 5 actionable items (combined, not per type) from both courses and gigs/opportunities that most directly address the user's skill gaps.\n\n- Order of priority for items\n\n    1. Direct match to a Skill Gap (title, description, or explanation must match a Skill Gap; do not infer loosely).\n    2. Earlier start date (if available and applicable).\n    3. Higher relevance score (if provided; otherwise, omit this criterion).\n\n- Available Actions \n    1. Action Name : Apply\n        - Applicable only for gigs\n        - Action Code: APPLY\n        - FollowUpCommandPayload:\n            ora.Invoke(\"APPLY\", {\"actionCode\": \"APPLY\", \"OpportunityId\": \"<OpportunityId>\", \"title\": <Title>})\n        - If priority = true:\n            - ActionText: \"Apply\"\n            - Title: Apply for <Gig Title> \n            - ShortDescription: 10 word description of the Gig\n        - If priority = false:\n            - ActionText: \"Apply for <Gig Title>\" \n            - Title: \"Apply for <Gig Title>\"\n\n    - Action Name : View Details\n        - Applicable only for Courses\n        - Action Code: \"VIEWCOURSE\"\n        - FollowUpCommandPayload : \n            ora.Invoke(\"VIEWCOURSE\", {\"actionCode\": \"VIEWCOURSE\", \"learningItemId\": \"<learningItemId>\", \"title\": <Course Title>})\n        - If priority = true:\n            - ActionText: \"Learn More\"\n            - Title: Learning Suggestion: <Course Title> \n            - ShortDescription: 10 word description of the Gig\n        - If priority = false:\n            - ActionText : \"Learning Suggestion: <Course Title>\"\n            - Title: \"Learning Suggestion: <Course Title>\"\n\n- Action Genration Directives\n\n    - For each selected item, provide exactly one of these actions based on user status\n    - Output a list (up to 5 items) of action objects that follow this schema\n\n{\n\"type\": \"object\",\n\"properties\": {\n\"title\": {\n\"type\": \"string\",\n\"description\": \"The main title of the notification. Must be a concise phrase, under 10 words.\"\n},\n\"shortDescription\": {\n\"type\": \"string\",\n\"description\": \"A brief description of the notification, written as a single, complete sentence.\"\n},\n\"actionText\": {\n\"type\": \"string\",\n\"description\": \"The text to display on the action button.\"\n},\n\"followUpCommand\": {\n\"type\": \"string\",\n\"description\": \"A command string to be executed. Must follow one of three standardized formats.\"\n},\n\"priority\": {\n\"type\": \"boolean\",\n\"description\": \"Optional. When true, the action is shown as a priority action.\"\n}\n},\n\"required\": [\"title\", \"shortDescription\", \"actionText\", \"followUpCommand\",priority],\n\"additionalProperties\": false\n}\n\n    - Refer to the Example Actions provided, do not take data from the example it it only for reference\n- Priority Distribution:\n    - Mark the top 2 actionable item as \"priority\": true.\n    - All other returned actions must have \"priority\": false`\n\n- Example Actions:\n\n[\n  {\n    \"actionText\": \"Learn More\",\n    \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\"VIEWCOURSE\", {\"actionCode\":\"VIEWCOURSE\",\"learningItemId\":<learningItemId>,\"title\":\"<Learning Item Title>\"})\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"<Short Description>\",\n    \"title\": \"Learning Suggestion: <Learning Item Title>\",\n    \"priority\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"actionText\": \"Apply\",\n    \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"APPLY\\\", {\\\"actionCode\\\": \\\"APPLY\\\", \\\"OpportunityId\\\": \\\"<GigId>\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"<Gig Title>\\\"})\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"<Short Description>.\",\n    \"title\": \"Apply for <Gig Title>\",\n    \"priority\": true\n  },\n  {\n    \"actionText\": \"Learning Suggestion: <Learning Item Title>\",\n    \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"VIEWCOURSE\\\", {\\\"actionCode\\\":\\\"VIEWCOURSE\\\",\\\"learningItemId\\\":<learningItemId>,\\\"title\\\":\\\"<Learning Item Title>\\\"})\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"Leverage techniques for optimizing deep learning models and implementing them using Python.\",\n    \"title\": \"Learning Suggestion: <Learning Item Title>\",\n    \"priority\": false\n  },\n  {\n    \"actionText\": \"Apply for <Gig Title>\",\n    \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"APPLY\\\", {\\\"actionCode\\\": \\\"APPLY\\\", \\\"OpportunityId\\\": \\\"<GigId>\\\", \\\"title\\\": \\\"<Gig Title>\\\"})\",\n    \"shortDescription\": \"<Short Ddescription>.\",\n    \"title\": \"Apply for <Gig Title>\",\n    \"priority\": false\n  }\n]\n\n- Guidelines\n\n    - Only match recommendations that directly address a Skill Gap; do not infer indirect matches.\n    - Only present one action per recommendation.\n    - Do not include explanations, justifications, or extra commentary outside of what is defined in your instructions.\n    - Use only the specified action types and codes: `APPLY`, `VIEWCOURSE`.\n    - Ensure the payload for `followUpCommand` always contains actionCode as the first parameter, and always includes the <Title> field with the title of the selected course or gig.\n    - Use field names and values from the provided data.\n    - If fewer than 5 items qualify, return only those.\n    - Preserve all field order and naming as in the output schema.\n    - Title should always be in Title Case\n    - Truncate the Name of Course or Gig if the Action Text or Title exceed 20 characters in the actions with priority = false\n    - The Examples do not represent real data, DO NOT use the example action data to generate actions. Only use the format of from the examples."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
